window.EXAM_DATA = {"id":"t3","title":"Topic 3 · completo","title_es":"Topic 3 · todas las preguntas (incluye secuenciales y Case Studies del Topic)","cases":{"CS1":{"title":"Case Study: Northwind Traders","en":"<h4>Background</h4>\n<p>Northwind Traders is an independent, family-owned business. The company distributes natural pet products in the Northwest region of the country/region. Products are purchased directly from manufacturers and distributed by using its own fleet of trucks.</p>\n<p>When the company started, deliveries were within a three-hour radius of the warehouse. Due to regional growth, current deliveries require drivers to stay overnight on some routes. The company plans to open a second warehouse to expand the region and eliminate overnights for route drivers. The company also plans to hire a second group of employees to run operations in this new location. The finance and accounting teams will remain in the original location.</p>\n<p>The company uses a third-party system for financials and order management. The finance department stated that the company's fiscal year begins on July 1 and ends on June 30. The mm/dd/yyyy date format is used.</p>\n<p>As part of the expansion, the owner plans to upgrade to an ERP system and use Business Central to fulfill the company requirements and manage growth.</p>\n<h4>Current environment</h4>\n<p><b>Orders</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Orders are emailed to customer service and manually keyed into the inventory system.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Pricing and discounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer pricing is determined by the customer market type. Customer market types are Retail, Veterinarian, and Breeder. Each customer is associated with only one market type.</li>\n<li>Vendors offer monthly promotions to customers by item, brand, or item category.</li>\n<li>Invoices should show each customer's base price, the discount amount, and the net price.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounts payable</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company wants to expand vendor payment options in the new system.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Requirements</h4>\n<p><b>Customers</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sales team must be able to: quickly set up new customers with the proper settings based on customer type; identify customers by market type. Customer posting groups will be used to identify which market the customer belongs to.</li>\n<li>Base price is determined by the customer market type.</li>\n<li>The sales department should receive a warning when entering the order if a customer is over their credit limit.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Sales</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer discounts are offered for specific time frames by item, brand, or product category. Discounts should be added to sales lines automatically.</li>\n<li>Discounts must post to a unique general ledger (G/L) account.</li>\n<li>The business needs to be able to track revenue by location, market, and product category dimensions. Locations 100 and 200 will be set as default dimensions on the two warehouse locations. Food, treats, toys, and supplies are the required product categories, which will be set as default dimensions on the item cards. Each customer card will have a default market dimension.</li>\n<li>The sales manager wants to delete canceled orders and automatically archive them.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Warehouse</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Orders will be fulfilled from two possible warehouse locations.</li>\n<li>Product will be transferred between locations by using transfer orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Sales invoices</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Invoices will be posted after delivery.</li>\n<li>Invoices will be emailed to the customer.</li>\n<li>The sales department must be able to quickly correct posted invoices for: posted invoices that have not been paid; posted invoices that have been paid; posted invoices created from sales orders; posted invoices not created from sales orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The finance department requires that the company has 12 monthly accounting periods per fiscal year.</li>\n<li>Finance department users must be able to reconcile the accounts receivable (AR) subledger to the G/L account at month end.</li>\n<li>AR department users need the ability to settle and close invoices when customers take payment discounts after the payment discount date has passed. AR users should be allowed to accept or reject the payment tolerance.</li>\n<li>Accounts payable (AP) department users must be able to pay vendors by electronic funds transfer (EFT) and use a payment journal batch named EFT to process payments.</li>\n<li>When viewing G/L entries, the finance and accounting teams must be able to see debits and credits instead of a positive or negative amount.</li>\n<li>The company needs to be able to track expenses by department and location. The departments are sales, operations, and administration.</li>\n<li>AR must be able to correct cash application entries.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Issues</h4>\n<p><b>Payment application</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customers may have several stores that are responsible for their own orders and payments.</li>\n<li>Occasionally, AR clerks mistakenly apply payments to the incorrect customer invoice.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>When items are delivered, customers refuse the items for reasons such as damaged or wrong item.</li>\n<li>After the invoices are posted, they must be corrected, which is time-consuming.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Warehouse</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The sales department and warehouse managers must have visibility into products that are in the process of being transferred between locations.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer accounts are difficult to view by market type.</li>\n<li>The finance team does not have the ability to report revenue by customer type.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Accounting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>AR users often find variances between the AR subledger and G/L account.</li>\n<li>Customers often take the payment discount after the payment discount date has passed, leaving open invoices for small amounts.</li>\n<li>The AP department is unable to pay vendors by EFT in the current system.</li>\n<li>Finance and accounting team members have trouble validating postings when they use only the amounts field on G/L entries.</li>\n<li>The finance department is unable to run financial reports by market. All revenue postings must reference a market.</li>\n</ul>","es":"<h4>Contexto</h4>\n<p>Northwind Traders es una empresa familiar independiente que distribuye productos naturales para mascotas en la región noroeste del país. Compra directamente a los fabricantes y reparte con su propia flota de camiones.</p>\n<p>Al principio, las entregas estaban a menos de tres horas del almacén. Con el crecimiento, algunas rutas obligan a los conductores a pasar la noche fuera. La empresa va a abrir un segundo almacén para ampliar la región y evitar esas noches, y contratará otro equipo para operar en la nueva ubicación. Finanzas y contabilidad seguirán en la ubicación original.</p>\n<p>Hoy usa un sistema de terceros para finanzas y gestión de pedidos. Su ejercicio (fiscal year) empieza el 1 de julio y termina el 30 de junio. Se usa el formato de fecha mm/dd/yyyy.</p>\n<p>Con la expansión, el propietario quiere pasar a un ERP y usar Business Central.</p>\n<h4>Entorno actual</h4>\n<p><b>Pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Los pedidos llegan por email a atención al cliente y se teclean a mano en el sistema de inventario.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Precios y descuentos</b></p><ul><li>El precio depende del tipo de mercado del cliente: Retail, Veterinarian y Breeder. Cada cliente pertenece a un solo mercado.</li><li>Los proveedores ofrecen promociones mensuales por producto, marca o categoría.</li><li>Las facturas deben mostrar el precio base, el importe del descuento y el precio neto.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas a pagar</b></p><ul><li>La empresa quiere ampliar las formas de pago a proveedores en el nuevo sistema.</li></ul>\n<h4>Requisitos</h4>\n<p><b>Clientes</b></p><ul><li>El equipo de ventas debe poder dar de alta clientes rápidamente con la configuración correcta según su tipo e identificar a los clientes por mercado. Se usarán los customer posting groups para identificar el mercado de cada cliente.</li><li>El precio base depende del mercado del cliente.</li><li>Ventas debe recibir un aviso al introducir el pedido si el cliente supera su límite de crédito.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Ventas</b></p><ul><li>Los descuentos se ofrecen durante periodos concretos por producto, marca o categoría y deben añadirse automáticamente a las líneas de venta.</li><li>Los descuentos deben registrarse en una cuenta contable (G/L) propia.</li><li>Hay que analizar los ingresos por las dimensiones ubicación, mercado y categoría de producto. Las ubicaciones 100 y 200 serán default dimensions de los dos almacenes; las categorías Food, Treats, Toys y Supplies serán default dimensions en las fichas de producto; cada cliente tendrá una dimensión de mercado por defecto.</li><li>El jefe de ventas quiere borrar los pedidos cancelados y archivarlos automáticamente.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Almacén</b></p><ul><li>Los pedidos se servirán desde dos almacenes posibles.</li><li>Los productos se moverán entre almacenes con transfer orders.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturas de venta</b></p><ul><li>Las facturas se registrarán después de la entrega.</li><li>Se enviarán al cliente por email.</li><li>Ventas debe poder corregir rápidamente facturas registradas: no pagadas, pagadas, creadas desde pedidos de venta y no creadas desde pedidos.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Contabilidad</b></p><ul><li>Finanzas necesita 12 periodos contables mensuales por ejercicio.</li><li>Finanzas debe poder conciliar a fin de mes el subledger de clientes (AR) con la cuenta contable.</li><li>AR debe poder liquidar y cerrar facturas cuando el cliente se toma el descuento por pronto pago después de la fecha de descuento, pudiendo aceptar o rechazar la tolerancia.</li><li>Cuentas a pagar (AP) debe poder pagar por transferencia electrónica (EFT) usando una sección del diario de pagos llamada EFT.</li><li>Al ver los movimientos contables, finanzas quiere ver debe y haber en lugar de importes positivos o negativos.</li><li>Hay que analizar los gastos por departamento (ventas, operaciones, administración) y ubicación.</li><li>AR debe poder corregir aplicaciones de cobros.</li></ul>\n<h4>Problemas</h4>\n<p><b>Aplicación de pagos</b></p><ul><li>Algunos clientes tienen varias tiendas responsables de sus propios pedidos y pagos.</li><li>A veces AR aplica los pagos a la factura equivocada.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Al entregar, los clientes rechazan productos (dañados, equivocados…).</li><li>Después de registrar las facturas hay que corregirlas, lo que lleva mucho tiempo.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Almacén</b></p><ul><li>Ventas y los responsables de almacén deben ver los productos que se están transfiriendo entre almacenes.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas</b></p><ul><li>Es difícil ver las cuentas de clientes por mercado.</li><li>Finanzas no puede informar de los ingresos por tipo de cliente.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Contabilidad</b></p><ul><li>AR encuentra a menudo diferencias entre el subledger de clientes y la cuenta contable.</li><li>Los clientes se toman el descuento después de la fecha, dejando facturas abiertas por importes pequeños.</li><li>AP no puede pagar por EFT con el sistema actual.</li><li>Finanzas tiene problemas para validar registros usando solo el campo Amount de los G/L entries.</li><li>Finanzas no puede sacar informes por mercado. Todos los registros de ingresos deben llevar un mercado.</li></ul>"},"CS2":{"title":"Case Study: Fabrikam, Inc.","en":"<h4>Background</h4>\n<p>Fabrikam, Inc., is a manufacturer of products for the gift industry. The company plans to implement Business Central as its new enterprise resource planning (ERP) system.</p>\n<p>The company sells to two types of customers: wholesale and retail. Retail customers order at special events and online. Wholesale customers send in orders by email.</p>\n<h4>Current Environment</h4>\n<p><b>Order processing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company uses a purchase order (PO) workflow for any PO over $500.</li>\n<li>The system has been fully configured for sales order prepayments and will check for a prepayment invoice at posting.</li>\n<li>Customers can special order products with a prepayment that is due on receipt.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Wholesale customer payment terms are net 30, with a 2% discount if paid within 10 days.</li>\n<li>Retail customer payment terms are payable on receipt or shipment.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Reporting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company uses headcount (number of employees) and square footage for statistical accounts.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Integrations</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company currently uses Outlook, Excel, Word, and Teams to communicate internally and externally with customers and vendors.</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Requirements</h4>\n<p><b>Order processing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>The company must be able to combine multiple purchase receipts into one vendor invoice.</li>\n<li>Posted vendor invoices must be reverted when damages are reported or a product is returned to the vendor.</li>\n<li>Fully invoiced POs must not appear on the PO list page.</li>\n<li>Customer prepayments vary based on customer relationship. Special orders from new customers have a 25% prepayment. Established customers have only a 15% prepayment.</li>\n<li>The company must be able to approve POs by email without opening Business Central.</li>\n<li>Customers often reorder the same items with similar quantities. The system must be configured to ask the user if recurring lines should be added to sales orders.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Invoicing</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Customer revenue must be posted to separate general ledger (G/L) accounts based on customer type. The G/L account must have subcategories for wholesale and retail revenue.</li>\n<li>Accounts receivable must be posted to separate G/L accounts based on customer type. The G/L account must have subcategories for wholesale and retail accounts receivable.</li>\n<li>Currently, inventory is sold at a cost based on purchase and sales over a period.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Reporting</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Financial reports must include statistical accounts.</li>\n<li>The financial report structure must map to account categories.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>Integrations</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Create sales orders while collaborating with customers by email.</li>\n<li>Edit customer information while messaging the sales team in a group chat.</li>\n<li>Communicate a brochure to all customers at once about a sales campaign.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><b>General ledger posting accounts</b></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Retail Receivables = 13100</li>\n<li>Wholesale Receivables = 13200</li>\n<li>Payment Discount = 54800</li>\n<li>Retail Sales = 44100</li>\n<li>Wholesale Sales = 44200</li>\n<li>Sales Prepayments = 22160</li>\n</ul>\n<h4>Issues</h4>\n<ul>\n<li>Order entry takes too long for wholesale customers.</li>\n<li>Vendors ship partial orders but send one monthly invoice. The company is unable to associate one invoice with multiple POs in the current environment.</li>\n<li>Inventory reconciliation was difficult in the company's old system because it allowed users to sell more inventory than was physically available.</li>\n<li>Users must log in to the system to provide workflow approvals.</li>\n</ul>","es":"<h4>Contexto</h4>\n<p>Fabrikam, Inc. fabrica productos para la industria del regalo y va a implantar Business Central como nuevo ERP.</p>\n<p>Vende a dos tipos de clientes: mayoristas (wholesale) y minoristas (retail). Los minoristas compran en eventos especiales y online; los mayoristas envían los pedidos por email.</p>\n<h4>Entorno actual</h4>\n<p><b>Procesamiento de pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Hay un workflow de pedidos de compra (PO) para cualquier PO de más de 500 $.</li><li>El sistema está configurado para anticipos (prepayments) en pedidos de venta y comprueba la factura de anticipo al registrar.</li><li>Los clientes pueden hacer pedidos especiales con un anticipo pagadero a la recepción.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Clientes mayoristas: neto a 30 días, con un 2 % de descuento si pagan en 10 días.</li><li>Clientes minoristas: pago a la recepción o al envío.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Informes</b></p><ul><li>Usa la plantilla (número de empleados) y los metros cuadrados como cuentas estadísticas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Integraciones</b></p><ul><li>Usa Outlook, Excel, Word y Teams para comunicarse interna y externamente.</li></ul>\n<h4>Requisitos</h4>\n<p><b>Procesamiento de pedidos</b></p><ul><li>Debe poder combinar varias recepciones de compra en una sola factura de proveedor.</li><li>Las facturas de proveedor registradas deben revertirse si hay daños o se devuelve el producto.</li><li>Los pedidos de compra totalmente facturados no deben aparecer en la lista de pedidos.</li><li>El anticipo depende de la relación con el cliente: pedidos especiales de clientes nuevos 25 %; clientes habituales solo 15 %.</li><li>Debe poder aprobar pedidos de compra por email sin abrir Business Central.</li><li>Los clientes suelen repetir los mismos productos con cantidades parecidas: el sistema debe preguntar si añadir las líneas recurrentes a los pedidos de venta.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Facturación</b></p><ul><li>Los ingresos deben registrarse en cuentas distintas según el tipo de cliente, con subcategorías para mayorista y minorista.</li><li>Las cuentas a cobrar deben registrarse en cuentas distintas según el tipo de cliente, con subcategorías para mayorista y minorista.</li><li>Hoy el inventario se vende a un coste basado en compras y ventas de un periodo.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Informes</b></p><ul><li>Los informes financieros deben incluir cuentas estadísticas.</li><li>La estructura del informe financiero debe corresponder a las categorías de cuentas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Integraciones</b></p><ul><li>Crear pedidos de venta mientras se colabora con clientes por email.</li><li>Editar datos de clientes mientras se chatea con el equipo de ventas en un chat de grupo.</li><li>Enviar a la vez a todos los clientes un folleto sobre una campaña de ventas.</li></ul>\n<p><b>Cuentas contables</b></p><ul><li>Retail Receivables = 13100</li><li>Wholesale Receivables = 13200</li><li>Payment Discount = 54800</li><li>Retail Sales = 44100</li><li>Wholesale Sales = 44200</li><li>Sales Prepayments = 22160</li></ul>\n<h4>Problemas</h4><ul><li>La introducción de pedidos de mayoristas es demasiado lenta.</li><li>Los proveedores envían pedidos parciales pero una sola factura mensual; hoy no se puede asociar una factura a varios pedidos.</li><li>La conciliación de inventario era difícil porque el sistema permitía vender más de lo que había físicamente.</li><li>Los usuarios deben entrar en el sistema para aprobar los workflows.</li></ul>"}},"questions":[{"id":"t3q1","type":"mc","en":"A company records vendor-wise item descriptions.<br><br>You need to set up vendor-specific descriptions for items.<br><br>What should you set up?","es":"Una empresa registra descripciones de productos distintas para cada proveedor.<br><br>Debes configurar descripciones de producto específicas por proveedor. ¿Qué debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Item variants","es":"Item variants (variantes de producto)"},{"id":"B","en":"Substitutions","es":"Substitutions (sustitutos)"},{"id":"C","en":"Item cross-references","es":"Item cross-references (referencias cruzadas de producto)"},{"id":"D","en":"Extended text","es":"Extended text (texto adicional)"}]},{"id":"t3q2","type":"hotspot","en":"A furniture manufacturing company is creating new items in Dynamics 365 Business Central. The company currently searches for the products by material, color, and size.<br><br>You must expand the search capabilities for the items. Not all the items will have the same searchable characteristics. Some new search characteristics may need to be added.<br><br>You need to configure the system to automatically recommend additional search criteria for items.<br><br>Which features should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un fabricante de muebles crea artículos nuevos. Hoy busca los productos por material, color y tamaño, pero no todos los artículos tienen las mismas características y pueden hacer falta otras nuevas.<br><br>Debes configurar el sistema para que recomiende automáticamente nuevos criterios de búsqueda. ¿Qué funcionalidad debes usar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 3 · Q2","rowsHeader":["Requirement","Feature"],"rows":[{"en":"Identify search criteria","es":"Identificar los criterios de búsqueda","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Item categories","es":"Item categories"},{"id":"b","en":"Item attributes","es":"Item attributes"},{"id":"c","en":"Item dimensions","es":"Item dimensions"},{"id":"d","en":"Cross references","es":"Cross references"}]},{"en":"Recommend new search criteria","es":"Recomendar nuevos criterios de búsqueda","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Essential Business Insights","es":"Essential Business Insights"},{"id":"b","en":"Item templates","es":"Item templates"},{"id":"c","en":"Analyze Data by Dimensions","es":"Analyze Data by Dimensions"},{"id":"d","en":"Image Analyzer","es":"Image Analyzer"}]}]},{"id":"t3q3","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central. The company has three sites.<br><br>The company needs to track inventory separately for each site.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet this requirement.<br><br>What should you configure?","es":"Una empresa tiene tres centros y necesita controlar el inventario de cada uno por separado.<br><br>¿Qué debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q3","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Warehouse","es":"Warehouse"},{"id":"B","en":"In-Transit location","es":"In-Transit location (almacén en tránsito)"},{"id":"C","en":"Location","es":"Location (almacén)"},{"id":"D","en":"Responsibility center","es":"Responsibility center (centro de responsabilidad)"}]},{"id":"t3q4","type":"mr","en":"A company operates from India. The company procures materials from Sweden.<br><br>You need to set up invoice discount terms for a vendor based in Sweden.<br><br>Which three pieces of information should you enter? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa de la India compra materiales en Suecia.<br><br>Debes configurar las condiciones de invoice discount (descuento en factura) de un proveedor sueco. ¿Qué tres datos debes introducir?","src":"Topic 3 · Q4","options":[{"id":"A","en":"currency code","es":"currency code (código de divisa)"},{"id":"B","en":"minimum amount","es":"minimum amount (importe mínimo)"},{"id":"C","en":"discount percentage","es":"discount percentage (% de descuento)"},{"id":"D","en":"starting date","es":"starting date (fecha inicial)"},{"id":"E","en":"minimum quantity","es":"minimum quantity (cantidad mínima)"}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q5","type":"mr","en":"A company configures special prices for a combination of an item number and a vendor.<br><br>You need to configure optional criteria for special pricing to calculate the best price for the combination.<br><br>Which three criteria should you use? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa configura precios especiales para la combinación de un producto y un proveedor.<br><br>Debes configurar criterios opcionales del precio especial para que el sistema calcule el mejor precio. ¿Qué tres criterios debes usar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q5","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Purchasing Code","es":"Purchasing Code"},{"id":"B","en":"Minimum Quantity","es":"Minimum Quantity"},{"id":"C","en":"Unit of Measure Code","es":"Unit of Measure Code"},{"id":"D","en":"Currency Code","es":"Currency Code"},{"id":"E","en":"Line Discount Percentage","es":"Line Discount Percentage"}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q6","type":"mr","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central for a customer who has two warehouses.<br><br>The customer requires the following:<ul><li>different item pricing and vendors set up for items in each warehouse</li><li>transactions tied to a specific location</li></ul>You need to configure Business Central per the customer requirements.<br><br>Which three entities should you configure? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un cliente tiene dos almacenes y necesita:<ul><li>precios y proveedores distintos para los productos de cada almacén</li><li>transacciones vinculadas a un almacén concreto</li></ul>¿Qué tres entidades debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q6","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Inventory setup","es":"Inventory Setup"},{"id":"B","en":"Warehouse setup","es":"Warehouse Setup"},{"id":"C","en":"Stockkeeping units","es":"Stockkeeping units (unidades de almacenamiento)"},{"id":"D","en":"Item card","es":"Item card (ficha de producto)"},{"id":"E","en":"Locations","es":"Locations (almacenes)"}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q7","type":"mc","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central. You create items for infinite items such as water, electricity, and natural gas that are used in manufacturing processes.<br><br>You need to set up the items.<br><br>Which item type should you use for infinite items?","es":"Creas productos para recursos \"infinitos\" como agua, electricidad o gas natural que se consumen en fabricación.<br><br>¿Qué tipo de producto (item type) debes usar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q7","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Resource","es":"Resource (recurso)"},{"id":"B","en":"Inventory","es":"Inventory"},{"id":"C","en":"Service","es":"Service"},{"id":"D","en":"Non-Inventory","es":"Non-Inventory"}]},{"id":"t3q8","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A customer requests that the company always use their preferred shipping provider for all sales orders.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet this requirement.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Un cliente pide que se use siempre su transportista preferido en todos sus pedidos de venta.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q8","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Select Shipping Advice","es":"Seleccionar Shipping Advice."},{"id":"B","en":"Define a shipping agent","es":"Definir un shipping agent."},{"id":"C","en":"Set up a Ship-to code","es":"Configurar un Ship-to code."},{"id":"D","en":"Designate a Responsibility center","es":"Asignar un Responsibility center."}]},{"id":"t3q9","type":"mr","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to manually add many similar items.<br><br>You need to help the customer create copies of existing items.<br><br>Which three actions must be performed? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Implantas Business Central y el cliente quiere crear manualmente muchos productos parecidos.<br><br>Debes ayudarle a crear copias de productos existentes. ¿Qué tres acciones hay que realizar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q9","options":[{"id":"A","en":"On the Set up Customer/Vendor/Item Templates page, create a new item template","es":"En la página de plantillas de cliente/proveedor/producto, crear una plantilla de producto nueva."},{"id":"B","en":"Open an existing item, and then click the Save as Template action on the item card","es":"Abrir un producto existente y usar la acción Save as Template en la ficha."},{"id":"C","en":"On the Set Up Customer/Vendor/Item Templates page, edit the information in the newly created item template","es":"En la página de plantillas, editar la información de la plantilla recién creada."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Configuration Templates page, create a new template for item table","es":"En la página Configuration Templates, crear una plantilla para la tabla de productos."},{"id":"E","en":"Create a new item, and then select the new template name to copy the information to the item","es":"Crear un producto nuevo y seleccionar la plantilla para copiar su información."}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q10","type":"drag","en":"You are configuring Dynamics 365 Business Central for a company.<br><br>You need to create items.<br><br>Which item types should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate item types to the correct scenarios. Each item type may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Estás configurando Business Central y debes crear artículos.<br><br>¿Qué tipo de artículo corresponde a cada escenario? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q10","valuesTitle":"Item types","targetHeader":["Scenario","Item type"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Inventory, non-inventory, and service","es":"Inventory, non-inventory, and service"},{"id":"V2","en":"Inventory only","es":"Inventory only"},{"id":"V3","en":"Non-Inventory only","es":"Non-Inventory only"},{"id":"V4","en":"Service only","es":"Service only"}],"targets":[{"en":"The item may be transferred between locations.","es":"El artículo puede transferirse entre ubicaciones."},{"en":"The item can be used in assembly consumption, but the quantity is not tracked.","es":"El artículo puede consumirse en ensamblados, pero no se controla su cantidad."},{"en":"Item will be used in sales transactions.","es":"El artículo se usará en ventas."}]},{"id":"t3q11","type":"mr","en":"You are implementing Dynamics 365 Business Central Online.<br><br>You receive a comprehensive price list from the customer. The customer wants you to set up the best price feature for sales by using the standard discount and pricing functionality in Business Central.<br><br>You need to set up this feature.<br><br>Which three components are part of the best price calculation feature? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Implantas Business Central Online. El cliente te da una lista de precios completa y quiere usar el cálculo del mejor precio (best price) con la funcionalidad estándar de precios y descuentos.<br><br>¿Qué tres componentes forman parte del cálculo del mejor precio?","src":"Topic 3 · Q11","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Unit cost on items","es":"Unit cost de los productos"},{"id":"B","en":"Sales Line Discounts","es":"Sales Line Discounts"},{"id":"C","en":"Vendor Discount Groups","es":"Vendor Discount Groups"},{"id":"D","en":"Special Prices","es":"Special Prices"},{"id":"E","en":"Unit prices on items","es":"Unit prices de los productos"}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q12","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to sell items in boxes and pallets, but refer to the items as pieces. Each box contains 12 pieces. Each pallet contains 144 pieces.<br><br>You need to assign the unit of measures to items.<br><br>How should you assign the unit of measures?","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente vende productos en cajas y palés, pero se refiere a ellos en piezas. Cada caja contiene 12 piezas y cada palé 144 piezas.<br><br>Debes asignar las unidades de medida a los productos. ¿Cómo debes hacerlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q12","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create Box as a base unit of measure. Add Pieces as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.08333.","es":"Crear Box como unidad base y añadir Pieces con cantidad por unidad 0,08333."},{"id":"B","en":"Create Pieces as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Pieces as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad base y añadir Box como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 12."},{"id":"D","en":"Create Pallet as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.08333.","es":"Crear Pallet como unidad base y añadir Box con cantidad por unidad 0,08333."}]},{"id":"t3q13","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A vendor needs to use a default warehouse location and invoice a different vendor for a purchase order.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet the requirements.<br><br>Which controls should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un proveedor debe usar un almacén de recepción por defecto y facturar a través de otro proveedor.<br><br>¿Qué control debes usar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 3 · Q13","rowsHeader":["Requirement","Control"],"rows":[{"en":"Configure the default receiving warehouse.","es":"Configurar el almacén de recepción por defecto.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Location Code","es":"Location Code"},{"id":"b","en":"Responsibility Center","es":"Responsibility Center"},{"id":"c","en":"Purchaser Code","es":"Purchaser Code"},{"id":"d","en":"Shipment Method Code","es":"Shipment Method Code"}]},{"en":"Configure the invoice address.","es":"Configurar la dirección de facturación.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Vendor No. (Pay to Vendor) on the Invoicing FastTab","es":"Vendor No. (Pay to Vendor) on the Invoicing FastTab"},{"id":"b","en":"Vendor Order Address on the Vendor Order Addresses","es":"Vendor Order Address on the Vendor Order Addresses"},{"id":"c","en":"Apply Template on the vendor card","es":"Apply Template on the vendor card"},{"id":"d","en":"Company level Contact on the contact card","es":"Company level Contact on the contact card"}]}]},{"id":"t3q14","type":"drag","en":"You set up a sales module for a company. The manager provides you with the company sales price list.<br><br>The correct net price for products must display when the sales team creates sales orders.<br><br>You need to configure the system.<br><br>Which setup types should you use? To answer, drag the appropriate setup types to the correct scenarios. Each setup type may be used once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Configuras ventas. El responsable te da la lista de precios y el precio neto correcto debe aparecer al crear pedidos.<br><br>¿Qué tipo de configuración corresponde a cada escenario? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q14","valuesTitle":"Setup types","targetHeader":["Scenario","Setup type"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Sales Prices","es":"Sales Prices"},{"id":"V2","en":"Unit Price","es":"Unit Price"},{"id":"V3","en":"Sales Line Discounts","es":"Sales Line Discounts"},{"id":"V4","en":"Customer Invoice Discounts","es":"Customer Invoice Discounts"}],"targets":[{"en":"The company offers different discounts for different item types.","es":"La empresa ofrece descuentos distintos según el tipo de artículo."},{"en":"Loyal customers are rewarded with additional discounts when a certain sales amount on an order is reached.","es":"Los clientes fieles reciben un descuento adicional al superar un importe en el pedido."},{"en":"Certain customers receive special prices for a certain amount of time.","es":"Ciertos clientes tienen precios especiales durante un tiempo."}]},{"id":"t3q16","type":"hotspot","en":"You create a new item in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure item settings.<br><br>Which item settings should you use? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Creas un artículo nuevo en Business Central y debes configurarlo.<br><br>¿Qué configuración del artículo corresponde a cada requisito?","src":"Topic 3 · Q16","rowsHeader":["Business requirement","Item setting"],"rows":[{"en":"Items must be interchangeable.","es":"Los artículos deben ser intercambiables.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Cross references","es":"Cross references"},{"id":"b","en":"Identifiers","es":"Identifiers"},{"id":"c","en":"Substitutions","es":"Substitutions"},{"id":"d","en":"Variants","es":"Variants"}]},{"en":"Multiple characteristics can be assigned to an item.","es":"Se pueden asignar varias características a un artículo.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Attributes","es":"Attributes"},{"id":"b","en":"Cross references","es":"Cross references"},{"id":"c","en":"Item category","es":"Item category"},{"id":"d","en":"Variants","es":"Variants"}]},{"en":"Items may be grouped and arranged.","es":"Los artículos se pueden agrupar y ordenar.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Attributes","es":"Attributes"},{"id":"b","en":"Item category","es":"Item category"},{"id":"c","en":"Stockkeeping units","es":"Stockkeeping units"},{"id":"d","en":"Variants","es":"Variants"}]},{"en":"Different locations may be replenished in different ways.","es":"Cada ubicación puede reaprovisionarse de forma distinta.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Item attributes","es":"Item attributes"},{"id":"b","en":"Item category","es":"Item category"},{"id":"c","en":"Stockkeeping units","es":"Stockkeeping units"},{"id":"d","en":"Substitutions","es":"Substitutions"}]}]},{"id":"t3q17","type":"drag","en":"You are setting up a new item in Dynamics 365 Business Central. The item is a tangible good with an inventory asset value. The item is acquired by purchase specifically for each new instance of demand from an order.<br><br>You need to configure the Type, Replenishment System, and Reordering Policy fields on the item card to achieve the stated requirements.<br><br>How should you configure each field? To answer, drag the appropriate values to the correct fields. Each value may be used once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Creas un producto nuevo: es un bien tangible con valor de inventario y se compra específicamente para cada nueva demanda de un pedido.<br><br>Debes configurar los campos Type, Replenishment System y Reordering Policy de la ficha de producto. ¿Qué valor corresponde a cada campo? Cada valor puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q17","valuesTitle":"Values","targetHeader":["Field","Value"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Inventory","es":"Inventory"},{"id":"V2","en":"Service","es":"Service"},{"id":"V3","en":"Non-Inventory","es":"Non-Inventory"},{"id":"V4","en":"Order","es":"Order"},{"id":"V5","en":"Lot-for-Lot","es":"Lot-for-Lot"},{"id":"V6","en":"Purchase","es":"Purchase"},{"id":"V7","en":"Transfer","es":"Transfer"},{"id":"V8","en":"Assembly","es":"Assembly"}],"targets":[{"en":"Type","es":"Type"},{"en":"Replenishment System","es":"Replenishment System"},{"en":"Reordering Policy","es":"Reordering Policy"}]},{"id":"t3q18","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A customer wants to sell items that are not normally counted in the company's warehouse.<br><br>You need to configure the system to meet this requirement.<br><br>What should you set up?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Un cliente quiere vender productos que normalmente no se cuentan en el almacén.<br><br>¿Qué debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q18","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Non-Inventory Item type","es":"Tipo de producto Non-Inventory"},{"id":"B","en":"Item charge","es":"Item charge"},{"id":"C","en":"Inventory Item type","es":"Tipo de producto Inventory"},{"id":"D","en":"Resource","es":"Resource"}]},{"id":"t3q19","type":"mr","en":"A company sells and services landscaping equipment.<br><br>The company wants to calculate an item's sales unit price based on a flat profit rate of 20 percent.<br><br>You need to adjust the item's unit price.<br><br>What are two possible ways to achieve the goal? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa vende y repara maquinaria de jardinería. Quiere calcular el precio de venta de un producto con un margen fijo del 20 %.<br><br>Debes ajustar el precio unitario del producto. ¿Cuáles son dos formas posibles de conseguirlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q19","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create a sales job price list for the specific item.","es":"Crear una lista de precios de venta de proyectos (job) para el producto."},{"id":"B","en":"Configure the unit price on the item card for the item.","es":"Configurar el precio unitario en la ficha del producto."},{"id":"C","en":"Create a sales price list for the specific item.","es":"Crear una lista de precios de venta para el producto."},{"id":"D","en":"Run the Adjust Item Costs/Prices batch job.","es":"Ejecutar el proceso Adjust Item Costs/Prices."},{"id":"E","en":"Configure the unit price by using the Suggest Item Price on Wksh feature.","es":"Configurar el precio con la función Suggest Item Price on Wksh."}],"select":2},{"id":"t3q20","type":"mr","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A purchaser receives a price list workbook from a vendor.<br><br>You need to upload prices to the system.<br><br>Which two types of price data can you load? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Un comprador recibe de un proveedor un libro de Excel con su lista de precios.<br><br>Debes cargar los precios en el sistema. ¿Qué dos tipos de datos de precio puedes cargar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q20","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Unit of Measure code","es":"Unit of Measure code"},{"id":"B","en":"Item No.","es":"Item No."},{"id":"C","en":"Customer price group","es":"Customer price group"},{"id":"D","en":"Campaign","es":"Campaign"}],"select":2},{"id":"t3q22","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to configure the system to automatically add any appropriate sales invoice discounts to sales documents.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Debes configurar el sistema para que añada automáticamente a los documentos de venta los invoice discounts (descuentos en factura) que correspondan.<br><br>¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q22","options":[{"id":"A","en":"On the Sales & Receivables Setup page, select Invoice Discount in Discount Posting.","es":"En Sales & Receivables Setup, seleccionar Invoice Discount en Discount Posting."},{"id":"B","en":"On the Sales & Receivables Setup page, select Calc. Inv. Discount.","es":"En Sales & Receivables Setup, activar Calc. Inv. Discount."},{"id":"C","en":"On the Customer card, select Invoice Disc. Code.","es":"En la ficha de cliente, seleccionar Invoice Disc. Code."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Sales & Receivables Setup page, select Lowest Price in Price Calculation Method.","es":"En Sales & Receivables Setup, seleccionar Lowest Price en Price Calculation Method."}]},{"id":"t3q23","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A vendor delivers items within one week after the company orders the items. The vendor ships the items by using a train.<br><br>You need to configure the vendor card.","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Un proveedor entrega los productos una semana después del pedido y los envía en tren.<br><br>Debes configurar la ficha del proveedor. ¿Qué campo usas?","src":"Topic 3 · Q23","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Base calendar code","es":"Base calendar code"},{"id":"B","en":"Lead time calculation","es":"Lead time calculation"},{"id":"C","en":"Location code","es":"Location code"},{"id":"D","en":"Shipment method code","es":"Shipment method code"}]},{"id":"t3q26","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>You need to ensure that sales invoice discounts are calculated automatically.<br><br>What should you configure?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. Debes asegurarte de que los descuentos de factura (invoice discounts) de venta se calculan automáticamente.<br><br>¿Qué debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q26","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Discount Posting setting on the Sales &amp; Receivables Setup page","es":"Discount Posting en Sales & Receivables Setup"},{"id":"B","en":"Calc. Inv. Discount setting on the Sales &amp; Receivables Setup page","es":"Calc. Inv. Discount en Sales & Receivables Setup"},{"id":"C","en":"Calc. Inv. Discount setting on the Purchase &amp; Payables Setup page","es":"Calc. Inv. Discount en Purchase & Payables Setup"},{"id":"D","en":"Show Amounts setting on the General Ledger Setup page","es":"Show Amounts en General Ledger Setup"}]},{"id":"t3q27","type":"hotspot","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company requires the following discount setup:<ul><li>The system must calculate the discounts given on individual items that are sold.</li><li>The system must post the discounts to a specific general ledger account.</li></ul>You need to configure the system.<br><br>Which settings should you configure? To answer, select the appropriate options in the answer area.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa necesita que el sistema calcule los descuentos concedidos en artículos vendidos y los registre en una cuenta contable concreta.<br><br>¿Qué configuración debes usar para cada requisito?","src":"Topic 3 · Q27","rowsHeader":["Requirement","Setting"],"rows":[{"en":"Calculate discounts given on items sold.","es":"Calcular los descuentos en artículos vendidos.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Select Line Discounts for the Discount Posting setting.","es":"Select Line Discounts for the Discount Posting setting."},{"id":"b","en":"Select Invoice Discounts for the Discount Posting setting.","es":"Select Invoice Discounts for the Discount Posting setting."},{"id":"c","en":"Select No Discounts for the Discount Posting setting.","es":"Select No Discounts for the Discount Posting setting."}]},{"en":"Post discounts to general ledger account.","es":"Registrar los descuentos en una cuenta contable.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Enter the G/L account for the Sales Line Disc. Account setting.","es":"Enter the G/L account for the Sales Line Disc. Account setting."},{"id":"b","en":"Enter the G/L account for the Sales Inv. Disc. Account setting.","es":"Enter the G/L account for the Sales Inv. Disc. Account setting."},{"id":"c","en":"Enter the G/L account for the Purch. Line Disc. Account setting.","es":"Enter the G/L account for the Purch. Line Disc. Account setting."}]}]},{"id":"t3q28","type":"mr","en":"A company implements Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company plans to automatically post inventory-related documents simultaneously when posting sales transactions.<br><br>You need to configure sales and receivables.<br><br>Which two settings should you use? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa implanta Business Central y quiere que, al registrar ventas, se registren automáticamente a la vez los documentos de inventario relacionados.<br><br>¿Qué dos opciones de ventas debes usar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q28","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Return Receipt on Credit Memo","es":"Return Receipt on Credit Memo"},{"id":"B","en":"Stock warning","es":"Stock warning"},{"id":"C","en":"Document Default Line Type","es":"Document Default Line Type"},{"id":"D","en":"Shipment on Invoice","es":"Shipment on Invoice"}],"select":2},{"id":"t3q30","type":"drag","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>Users in the purchasing and accounts payable departments require the following information about vendors and vendor ledger entries:<ul><li>Balance (LCY) for vendor</li><li>Remaining amount for ledger entry</li><li>Amount for application entry</li></ul>You need to retrieve the vendor and vendor ledger entry information.<br><br>Where should you navigate to find the information? To answer, drag the appropriate locations to the correct requirements. Each location may be used once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Compras y cuentas a pagar necesitan esta información de proveedores y movimientos de proveedor:<ul><li>Saldo (DL) del proveedor</li><li>Importe pendiente de un movimiento</li><li>Importe de una aplicación (liquidación)</li></ul>¿Dónde debes buscar cada dato? Cada ubicación puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q30","valuesTitle":"Locations","targetHeader":["Requirement","Location"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Vendor card","es":"Vendor card (ficha de proveedor)"},{"id":"V2","en":"Vendor ledger entries","es":"Vendor ledger entries (movimientos de proveedor)"},{"id":"V3","en":"Detailed vendor ledger entries","es":"Detailed vendor ledger entries (movimientos detallados de proveedor)"}],"targets":[{"en":"Balance (LCY) for vendor","es":"Saldo (DL) del proveedor"},{"en":"Remaining amount for ledger entry","es":"Importe pendiente de un movimiento"},{"en":"Amount for application entry","es":"Importe de una aplicación"}]},{"id":"t3q32","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to sell items in D, but refer to the items as pieces. Each box contains 12 pieces. Each pallet contains 144 pieces.<br><br>You need to assign the unit of measures to items.<br><br>How should you assign the unit of measures?","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente vende productos en cajas y palés, pero se refiere a ellos en piezas. Cada caja contiene 12 piezas y cada palé 144 piezas.<br><br>Debes asignar las unidades de medida a los productos. ¿Cómo debes hacerlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q32","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create Box as a base unit of measure. Add Pieces as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.08333.","es":"Crear Box como unidad base y añadir Pieces con cantidad por unidad 0,08333."},{"id":"B","en":"Create Pieces as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Pieces as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad base y añadir Box como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 12."},{"id":"D","en":"Create Pallet as a base unit of measure. Add Pallet as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Pallet como unidad base y añadir Pallet con cantidad por unidad 12."}]},{"id":"t3q33","type":"mr","en":"A global trading company maintains records of customer information in Business Central. The company frequently conducts international trade and works with customers who operate in different currencies.<br><br>You need to configure the system to invoice customers who use foreign currency.<br><br>Which two areas should you configure? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Una empresa de comercio internacional guarda sus clientes en Business Central y trabaja con clientes que operan en distintas divisas.<br><br>Debes configurar el sistema para facturar a clientes en divisa extranjera. ¿Qué dos sitios debes configurar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q33","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Customer Card","es":"Customer Card"},{"id":"B","en":"Sales Invoice","es":"Sales Invoice"},{"id":"C","en":"Vendor Card","es":"Vendor Card"},{"id":"D","en":"Adjust Exchange Rates","es":"Adjust Exchange Rates"}],"select":2},{"id":"t3q34","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>After you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.<br><br>You must streamline monthly invoicing by automating repetitive entries for monthly charges when managing subscriptions.<br><br>You need to add default general ledger (GL) accounts to a Customer Card.<br><br>Solution: Configure a Document Layout on the Customer Card.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Debes agilizar la facturación mensual automatizando las líneas que se repiten cada mes en la gestión de suscripciones.<br><br>Debes añadir cuentas contables (GL accounts) predeterminadas a la ficha del cliente.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> configurar un Document Layout en la ficha del cliente.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q34","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t3q35","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>After you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.<br><br>You must streamline monthly invoicing by automating repetitive entries for monthly charges when managing subscriptions.<br><br>You need to add default general ledger (GL) accounts to a Customer Card.<br><br>Solution: Apply a Microsoft Word template on the Customer Card.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Debes agilizar la facturación mensual automatizando las líneas que se repiten cada mes en la gestión de suscripciones.<br><br>Debes añadir cuentas contables (GL accounts) predeterminadas a la ficha del cliente.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> aplicar una plantilla de Microsoft Word en la ficha del cliente.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q35","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t3q36","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>After you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.<br><br>You must streamline monthly invoicing by automating repetitive entries for monthly charges when managing subscriptions.<br><br>You need to add default general ledger (GL) accounts to a Customer Card.<br><br>Solution: Configure the Standard Sales Lines Card and assign it to the Customer Card.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Debes agilizar la facturación mensual automatizando las líneas que se repiten cada mes en la gestión de suscripciones.<br><br>Debes añadir cuentas contables (GL accounts) predeterminadas a la ficha del cliente.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> configurar una ficha de <b>Standard Sales Lines</b> (Standard Sales Code) y asignarla a la ficha del cliente.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q36","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t3q41","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to sell items in boxes and pallets, but refer to the items as pieces. Each box contains 12 pieces. Each pallet contains 144 pieces.<br><br>You need to assign the unit of measures to items.<br><br>How should you assign the unit of measures?","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente vende productos en cajas y palés, pero se refiere a ellos en piezas. Cada caja contiene 12 piezas y cada palé 144 piezas.<br><br>Debes asignar las unidades de medida a los productos. ¿Cómo debes hacerlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q41","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create Pieces as a base unit of measure. Add Pallet as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 144.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad base y añadir Pallet como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 144."},{"id":"B","en":"Create Pieces as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Box as a base unit of measure. Add Pallet as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Box como unidad base y añadir Pallet con cantidad por unidad 12."},{"id":"D","en":"Create Pallet as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.08333.","es":"Crear Pallet como unidad base y añadir Box con cantidad por unidad 0,08333."}]},{"id":"t3q42","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company performs an annual review of customer prices and determines that sales prices must rise by 10% for the coming year.<br><br>You need to adjust the prices.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. En la revisión anual de precios decide que los precios de venta deben subir un 10 % el próximo año.<br><br>Debes ajustar los precios. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q42","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Use the action Copy Prices.","es":"Usar la acción Copy Prices."},{"id":"B","en":"Use the action Suggest Item Price on Worksheet.","es":"Usar la acción Suggest Item Price on Worksheet."},{"id":"C","en":"Implement price changes to the sales price worksheet.","es":"Implementar los cambios de precio de la hoja de precios de venta."},{"id":"D","en":"Manually add new lines to the Sales Lines Discount page.","es":"Añadir manualmente líneas nuevas en Sales Line Discounts."}]},{"id":"t3q44","type":"yn","en":"Note: This question is part of a series of questions that present the same scenario. Each question in the series contains a unique solution that might meet the stated goals. Some question sets might have more than one correct solution, while others might not have a correct solution.<br><br>After you answer a question in this section, you will NOT be able to return to it. As a result, these questions will not appear in the review screen.<br><br>You must streamline monthly invoicing by automating repetitive entries for monthly charges when managing subscriptions.<br><br>You need to add default general ledger (GL) accounts to a Customer Card.<br><br>Solution: Configure a Standard Purchase Code Card and assign it to a Vendor Card.<br><br>Does the solution meet the goal?","es":"<i>Nota: esta pregunta forma parte de una serie con el mismo escenario. Cada pregunta propone una solución distinta que podría cumplir el objetivo.</i><br><br>Debes agilizar la facturación mensual automatizando las líneas que se repiten cada mes en la gestión de suscripciones.<br><br>Debes añadir cuentas contables (GL accounts) predeterminadas a la ficha del cliente.<br><br><b>Solución:</b> configurar una ficha de Standard Purchase Code y asignarla a una ficha de proveedor.<br><br>¿Cumple la solución el objetivo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q44","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Yes","es":"Sí"},{"id":"B","en":"No","es":"No"}]},{"id":"t3q45","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to sell items in boxes and pallets, but refer to the items as pieces. Each box contains 12 pieces. Each pallet contains 144 pieces.<br><br>You need to assign the unit of measures to items.<br><br>How should you assign the unit of measures?","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente vende productos en cajas y palés, pero se refiere a ellos en piezas. Cada caja contiene 12 piezas y cada palé 144 piezas.<br><br>Debes asignar las unidades de medida a los productos. ¿Cómo debes hacerlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q45","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create Box as a base unit of measure. Add Pallet as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Box como unidad base y añadir Pallet con cantidad por unidad 12."},{"id":"B","en":"Create Pieces as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Pieces as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad base y añadir Box como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 12."},{"id":"D","en":"Create Boxes as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Boxes como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."}]},{"id":"t3q46","type":"drag","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The finance manager requires distinct processes for posting sales, purchase invoices, and shipments.<br><br>You need to configure the restrictions.<br><br>Which invoice posting policy should you use? To answer, move the appropriate invoice posting policies to the correct requirements. You may use each requirement once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"El responsable financiero quiere procesos distintos para registrar ventas, facturas de compra y envíos.<br><br>¿Qué invoice posting policy corresponde a cada requisito? Cada una puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q46","valuesTitle":"Invoice posting policies","targetHeader":["Requirement","Invoice posting policy"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Allowed","es":"Allowed"},{"id":"V2","en":"Mandatory","es":"Mandatory"},{"id":"V3","en":"Prohibited","es":"Prohibited"}],"targets":[{"en":"Allow the user to ship only from sales orders.","es":"Que el usuario solo pueda enviar desde los pedidos de venta."},{"en":"Force the user to post invoices together with receipts for purchase orders.","es":"Obligar a registrar la factura junto con la recepción de los pedidos de compra."},{"en":"Enable the user to ship or ship and invoice on inventory pick.","es":"Permitir enviar, o enviar y facturar, desde el picking."}]},{"id":"t3q47","type":"mr","en":"A manufacturer uses Dynamics 365 Business Central to procure items.<br><br>When the manufacturer deletes or changes purchase orders and blanket purchase orders, a record of these document changes must automatically be maintained. The configuration should not impact performance.<br><br>You need to configure Business Central to automatically record the changes.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un fabricante usa Business Central para comprar materiales. Cuando borra o modifica pedidos de compra y pedidos abiertos (blanket orders), debe guardarse automáticamente un registro de esos cambios sin afectar al rendimiento.<br><br>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q47","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Enable archiving of orders.","es":"Activar el archivo de pedidos (Archive Orders)."},{"id":"B","en":"Open the Sales &amp; Receivables Setup page.","es":"Abrir la página Sales & Receivables Setup."},{"id":"C","en":"Open the Purchases &amp; Payables Setup page.","es":"Abrir la página Purchases & Payables Setup."},{"id":"D","en":"Activate the change log.","es":"Activar el change log."},{"id":"E","en":"Enable archiving of blanket orders.","es":"Activar el archivo de pedidos abiertos (Archive Blanket Orders)."}],"select":3},{"id":"t3q49","type":"mc","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to sell items in boxes and pallets, but refer to the items as pieces. Each box contains 12 pieces. Each pallet contains 144 pieces.<br><br>You need to assign the unit of measures to items.<br><br>How should you assign the unit of measures?","es":"Configuras una company nueva. El cliente vende productos en cajas y palés, pero se refiere a ellos en piezas. Cada caja contiene 12 piezas y cada palé 144 piezas.<br><br>Debes asignar las unidades de medida a los productos. ¿Cómo debes hacerlo?","src":"Topic 3 · Q49","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create Pieces as an item unit of measure with a quantity per unit of measure set to 1.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 1."},{"id":"B","en":"Create Pallet as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.08333.","es":"Crear Pallet como unidad base y añadir Box con cantidad por unidad 0,08333."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Pallet as a base unit of measure. Add Pieces as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 0.0069.","es":"Crear Pallet como unidad base y añadir Pieces con cantidad por unidad 0,0069."},{"id":"D","en":"Create Pieces as a base unit of measure. Add Box as an item unit of measure with the quantity per unit set to 12.","es":"Crear Pieces como unidad base y añadir Box como unidad del producto con cantidad por unidad 12."}]},{"id":"t3q50","type":"drag","en":"A client uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The client must create a manufacturing company and a sales company in Business Central. Each company must be a separate legal entity.<br><br>The client must select a costing method to use.<br><br>You need to explain the effects of the different costing methods.<br><br>What should you describe for each costing method? To answer, move the appropriate effect to the correct costing method. You may use each effect once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to drag the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un cliente va a crear una company de fabricación y otra de ventas y debe elegir el método de valoración de existencias.<br><br>¿Qué efecto corresponde a cada costing method? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q50","valuesTitle":"Effects","targetHeader":["Costing method","Effect"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Use in businesses where product cost is unstable.","es":"Para empresas con costes de producto inestables."},{"id":"V2","en":"The unit cost of an item is the exact cost at which the particular unit was received.","es":"El coste unitario es el coste exacto con el que se recibió esa unidad."},{"id":"V3","en":"The unit cost of an item is preset based on estimated costs.","es":"El coste unitario se fija de antemano a partir de costes estimados."}],"targets":[{"en":"Average","es":"Average"},{"en":"Specific","es":"Specific"},{"en":"Standard","es":"Standard"}]},{"id":"t3q51","type":"mr","en":"You are setting up Business Central for a company.<br><br>The accounting manager requires the following setup for posted transactions:<ul><li>The use of locations must be mandatory for all users</li><li>Bins must be set up as mandatory for each location.</li></ul>You need to configure the system to meet the requirements.<br><br>Which two pages should you use? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"El responsable de contabilidad exige para las transacciones registradas:<ul><li>Uso obligatorio de locations (almacenes) para todos los usuarios.</li><li>Bins (ubicaciones) obligatorios en cada almacén.</li></ul>¿Qué dos páginas debes usar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q51","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Inventory Setup","es":"Inventory Setup"},{"id":"B","en":"Location Card","es":"Location Card (ficha de almacén)"},{"id":"C","en":"Inventory Posting Setup","es":"Inventory Posting Setup"},{"id":"D","en":"Sales & Receivables Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"},{"id":"E","en":"Item Card","es":"Item Card"}],"select":2},{"id":"t3q57","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company performs an annual review of customer prices and determines that sales prices must rise by 10% for the coming year.<br><br>You need to adjust the prices.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. En la revisión anual de precios decide que los precios de venta deben subir un 10 % el próximo año.<br><br>Debes ajustar los precios. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q57","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Manually add new lines to the Sales Lines Discount page.","es":"Añadir manualmente líneas nuevas en Sales Line Discounts."},{"id":"B","en":"Manually add a sales price to the Sales Price Worksheet page.","es":"Añadir manualmente un precio en la Sales Price Worksheet."},{"id":"C","en":"Use the action Suggest Sales Price on Worksheet.","es":"Usar la acción Suggest Sales Price on Worksheet."},{"id":"D","en":"Use the action Copy Prices.","es":"Usar la acción Copy Prices."}]},{"id":"t3q59","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company performs an annual review of customer prices and determines that sales prices must rise by 10% for the coming year.<br><br>You need to adjust the prices.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. En la revisión anual de precios decide que los precios de venta deben subir un 10 % el próximo año.<br><br>Debes ajustar los precios. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q59","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Manually add a sales price to the Sales Price Worksheet page.","es":"Añadir manualmente un precio en la Sales Price Worksheet."},{"id":"B","en":"Use the Adjust Item Costs/Prices function.","es":"Usar la función Adjust Item Costs/Prices."},{"id":"C","en":"Manually add new lines to the Sales Lines Discount page.","es":"Añadir manualmente líneas nuevas en Sales Line Discounts."},{"id":"D","en":"Use the action Suggest Item Price on Worksheet.","es":"Usar la acción Suggest Item Price on Worksheet."}]},{"id":"t3q60","type":"drag","en":"A heavy equipment dealership with two warehouses is implementing Business Central. One warehouse is for parts, and one is for equipment.<br><br>The dealership must separate inventory by the type of item and post to two general ledger (G/L) accounts:<ul><li>Parts inventory</li><li>Equipment Inventory</li></ul>You need to configure the system to post inventory to the correct G/L accounts.<br><br>Which components should you use? To answer, move the appropriate components to the correct configurations. You may use each component once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"Un concesionario de maquinaria con dos almacenes (recambios y equipos) debe separar el inventario por tipo de artículo y registrarlo en dos cuentas contables distintas.<br><br>¿Qué componente corresponde a cada configuración? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q60","valuesTitle":"Components","targetHeader":["Configuration","Component"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup"},{"id":"V2","en":"Inventory Posting Setup","es":"Inventory Posting Setup"},{"id":"V3","en":"Location","es":"Location"},{"id":"V4","en":"Item","es":"Item"}],"targets":[{"en":"Select inventory accounts for G/L posting.","es":"Seleccionar las cuentas de inventario para el registro contable."},{"en":"Combine with an inventory posting group to determine which G/L account to use during posting.","es":"Combinar con un inventory posting group para decidir qué cuenta usar."}]},{"id":"t3q61","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company performs an annual review of customer prices and determines that sales prices must rise by 10% for the coming year.<br><br>You need to adjust the prices.<br><br>What should you do?","es":"Una empresa usa Business Central. En la revisión anual de precios decide que los precios de venta deben subir un 10 % el próximo año.<br><br>Debes ajustar los precios. ¿Qué debes hacer?","src":"Topic 3 · Q61","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Manually add a sales price to the Sales Prices page.","es":"Añadir manualmente un precio en la página Sales Prices."},{"id":"B","en":"Manually add a sales price to the Sales Price Worksheet page.","es":"Añadir manualmente un precio en la Sales Price Worksheet."},{"id":"C","en":"Use the action Suggest Sales Price on Worksheet.","es":"Usar la acción Suggest Sales Price on Worksheet."},{"id":"D","en":"Use the action Copy Prices.","es":"Usar la acción Copy Prices."}]},{"id":"t3q62","type":"mc","en":"A large distribution company uses Business Central.<br><br>The volume of inventory transactions has tripled since its implementation. Users experience performance issues when posting transactions.<br><br>You need to review Inventory Setup and update the configuration.<br><br>Which configuration should you use?","es":"Una gran distribuidora usa Business Central. El volumen de transacciones de inventario se ha triplicado desde la implantación y los usuarios tienen problemas de rendimiento al registrar.<br><br>Debes revisar Inventory Setup y actualizar la configuración. ¿Cuál usas?","src":"Topic 3 · Q62","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Enable expected cost posting of G/L.","es":"Activar Expected Cost Posting to G/L."},{"id":"B","en":"Enable cost adjustment logging for all transactions.","es":"Activar el registro de ajustes de coste para todas las transacciones."},{"id":"C","en":"Configure automatic cost adjustment to never.","es":"Configurar Automatic Cost Adjustment = Never."},{"id":"D","en":"Configure automatic cost adjustment to always.","es":"Configurar Automatic Cost Adjustment = Always."}]},{"id":"t3q63","type":"drag","en":"You are implementing Business Central for a company.<br><br>The finance manager requires the following implementation to determine which customers are required to make a full or partial payment before items are shipped:<ul><li>Enable the same number series for prepayments as the one used for sales invoicing.</li><li>Establish default values for a required prepayment percentage for specific items and customers.</li><li>Automatically post prepayments to a designated G/L account.</li></ul>You need to recommend the component to use for each implementation requirement.<br><br>Which component should you use? To answer, move the appropriate components to the correct requirements. You may use each component once, more than once, or not at all.<br><br>NOTE: Each correct selection is worth one point.","es":"El responsable financiero quiere determinar qué clientes deben pagar total o parcialmente antes del envío (prepayments, prepagos):<ul><li>Usar para los prepagos la misma serie numérica que para las facturas de venta.</li><li>Definir porcentajes de prepago por defecto para clientes y productos concretos.</li><li>Registrar automáticamente los prepagos en una cuenta contable designada.</li></ul>¿Qué componente corresponde a cada requisito? Cada uno puede usarse una vez, varias o ninguna.","src":"Topic 3 · Q63","valuesTitle":"Components","targetHeader":["Action","Component"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Customer Card","es":"Customer Card"},{"id":"V2","en":"General Posting Setup","es":"General Posting Setup"},{"id":"V3","en":"General Ledger Setup","es":"General Ledger Setup"},{"id":"V4","en":"Sales & Receivables Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"}],"targets":[{"en":"Same number series for prepayments as for sales invoicing","es":"Misma serie numérica para prepagos que para facturas de venta"},{"en":"Default prepayment percentage values for specific items and customers","es":"Porcentajes de prepago por defecto para productos y clientes concretos"},{"en":"Automatic posting prepayments to designated G/L account","es":"Registro automático de prepagos en una cuenta contable designada"}]},{"id":"t3q64","type":"drag","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company records credit card fees on customer payments.<br><br>The company encounters issues with recording credit card payments and associated bank fees on customer payments in its financial system. The transactions must be accurately recorded in the Cash Receipt Journal to ensure proper accounting and reconciliation.<br><br>You need to configure the Cash Receipt Journal by selecting the appropriate account types to address the issues.<br><br>Which account types should you use? To answer, move the appropriate account types to the correct business requirements. You may use each account type once, more than once, or not at all. You may need to move the split bar between panes or scroll to view content.","es":"La empresa registra comisiones de tarjeta en los cobros de clientes y tiene problemas para registrar los cobros con tarjeta y las comisiones bancarias en el Cash Receipt Journal.<br><br>¿Qué tipo de cuenta corresponde a cada requisito?","src":"Topic 3 · Q64","valuesTitle":"Account types","targetHeader":["Business requirement","Account type"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Customer","es":"Customer"},{"id":"V2","en":"Bank Account","es":"Bank Account"},{"id":"V3","en":"G/L Account","es":"G/L Account"},{"id":"V4","en":"Vendor","es":"Vendor"}],"targets":[{"en":"Record a credit card payment received from a customer","es":"Registrar un cobro con tarjeta de un cliente"},{"en":"Register bank fees on a customer payment","es":"Registrar las comisiones bancarias de un cobro"}]},{"id":"t3q65","type":"mc","en":"A company uses Business Central.<br><br>The company made a mistake on a posted sales invoice and must correct it.<br><br>You need to validate whether you can correct the posted sales invoice or need to create a new corrective credit memo.<br><br>Which validation action should you do?","es":"La empresa cometió un error en una factura de venta registrada y debe corregirlo.<br><br>Debes comprobar si puedes corregir la factura registrada o si necesitas crear un abono correctivo. ¿Qué debes comprobar?","src":"Topic 3 · Q65","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Payment","es":"Payment (pago)"},{"id":"B","en":"Shipment","es":"Shipment (envío)"},{"id":"C","en":"Prepayment","es":"Prepayment (prepago)"}]},{"id":"s3q15","type":"build","en":"You are setting up a new company for a customer.<br><br>The customer wants to understand the structure of the elements involved in inventory posting.<br><br>You need to describe the relationship between elements in a basic inventory setup.<br><br>What is the hierarchical order of the elements included in inventory posting beginning with the master data? To answer, move the appropriate three entities from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.","es":"El cliente quiere entender la estructura de los elementos que intervienen en el registro de inventario.<br><br>¿Cuál es el orden jerárquico, empezando por los datos maestros? Mueve las tres entidades adecuadas y ordénalas.","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q15","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Stockkeeping Units","es":"Stockkeeping Units"},{"id":"B","en":"Value Entries","es":"Value Entries (movimientos de valor)"},{"id":"C","en":"Item Ledger Entries","es":"Item Ledger Entries (movimientos de producto)"},{"id":"D","en":"Warehouse Entries","es":"Warehouse Entries (movimientos de almacén)"},{"id":"E","en":"Items","es":"Items (productos)"}]},{"id":"s3q21","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The accounting manager wants partially shipped and invoiced sales orders that will not be fulfilled to not be displayed on the active page (Open Sales Order list). Deleted sales orders must be available for reporting of ordered and delivered quantities.<br><br>You need to configure sales orders.<br><br>In which order should you perform the actions? To answer, move all actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.","es":"El responsable contable quiere que los pedidos de venta parcialmente enviados y facturados que no se completarán no aparezcan en la lista de pedidos abiertos. Los pedidos eliminados deben seguir disponibles para informes de cantidades pedidas y entregadas.<br><br>¿En qué orden debes realizar todas las acciones?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q21","slots":5,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Change the sales order status to Released.","es":"Cambiar el estado del pedido a Released."},{"id":"B","en":"Enable Archive Sales Orders in Sales & Receivables Setup.","es":"Activar Archive Sales Orders en Sales & Receivables Setup."},{"id":"C","en":"Run the Delete Invoiced Sales Orders job.","es":"Ejecutar el proceso Delete Invoiced Sales Orders."},{"id":"D","en":"Change the sales order status to Open.","es":"Cambiar el estado del pedido a Open."},{"id":"E","en":"Reduce the sales order quantity to match the shipped quantity.","es":"Reducir la cantidad del pedido a la cantidad enviada."}]},{"id":"s3q24","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company bills thousands of sales invoices for recurring subscription services on a monthly basis.<br><br>You need to ensure recurring sales invoices are automatically created for the same subscription services.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"La empresa emite cada mes miles de facturas de suscripciones recurrentes.<br><br>Debes conseguir que las facturas recurrentes se creen automáticamente. ¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q24","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Update the Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices to Always Ask.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices en Always Ask."},{"id":"B","en":"Configure the Standard Sales Lines Card by defining the Code field, enter Subscription details and choose the appropriate G/L account.","es":"Configurar la Standard Sales Lines Card con su código, la suscripción y la cuenta contable."},{"id":"C","en":"Update the Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices to Manual.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices en Manual."},{"id":"D","en":"Open the Customer List page and select the customer for recurring billing services. Click on the customer, select Related, Sales, and then Recurring Sales Lines.","es":"Abrir la lista de clientes, elegir el cliente y abrir Related > Sales > Recurring Sales Lines."},{"id":"E","en":"Update the Insert Rec. Lines on Orders on Invoices to Automatic.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices en Automatic."},{"id":"F","en":"Assign the Standard Sales Lines Card to recurring subscription services.","es":"Asignar la Standard Sales Lines Card a las suscripciones recurrentes."},{"id":"G","en":"Run the Create Recurring Sales Invoices task batch job.","es":"Ejecutar el proceso Create Recurring Sales Invoices."}]},{"id":"s3q25","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A user creates two accounts for the same vendor. Both accounts have open vendor ledger entries.<br><br>You need to merge any open entries from the second vendor account to the first vendor account and then delete the second vendor account.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Un usuario ha creado dos fichas para el mismo proveedor y ambas tienen movimientos abiertos.<br><br>Debes pasar los movimientos abiertos de la segunda a la primera y eliminar la segunda. ¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q25","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"On the Vendor card, select Apply Template.","es":"En la ficha de proveedor, seleccionar Apply Template."},{"id":"B","en":"On the Merge Duplicated page, choose the Merge action.","es":"En la página Merge Duplicate, elegir Merge."},{"id":"C","en":"Select the duplicate customer in the Merge With field.","es":"Seleccionar el registro duplicado en el campo Merge With."},{"id":"D","en":"On the Vendor Card page, choose the Merge With action.","es":"En la Vendor Card, elegir la acción Merge With."}]},{"id":"s3q31","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>A maintenance manager buys weekly cleaning supplies from a local hardware store and would like to automate purchase order entries.<br><br>You need to configure the system to add a default general ledger (G/L) account to the hardware store purchase orders.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"Un responsable de mantenimiento compra cada semana productos de limpieza en una ferretería y quiere automatizar los pedidos.<br><br>Debes añadir por defecto una cuenta contable a los pedidos de ese proveedor. ¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q31","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Change the Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices to Automatic, and then close the window.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Invoices en Automatic y cerrar."},{"id":"B","en":"Change the Insert Rec. Lines on Orders to Automatic, and then close the window.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Orders en Automatic y cerrar."},{"id":"C","en":"Select Payment Terms code for the selected vendor.","es":"Seleccionar el Payment Terms Code del proveedor."},{"id":"D","en":"Configure Standard Purchase Code and set up relevant G/L account.","es":"Configurar un Standard Purchase Code con la cuenta contable."},{"id":"E","en":"Choose Standard Purchase Code for the selected vendor as a recurring purchase line.","es":"Asignar el Standard Purchase Code al proveedor como línea recurrente."}]},{"id":"s3q40","type":"build","en":"A company uses Business Central to manage retail product pricing and discounts. The new sales pricing experience has not been enabled.<br><br>The company plans to track discounts applied to sales transactions. The company has a specific price list for each customer.<br><br>You need to set up item discounts separately to meet business needs.<br><br>Which three actions should you perform in sequence? To answer, move the appropriate actions from the list of actions to the answer area and arrange them in the correct order.","es":"Una empresa gestiona precios y descuentos de venta en Business Central sin la nueva experiencia de precios activada. Tiene una lista de precios para cada cliente y quiere controlar los descuentos aplicados.<br><br>Debes configurar descuentos de producto por separado. ¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q40","slots":3,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Specify the customer who will receive a discount.","es":"Indicar el cliente que recibirá el descuento."},{"id":"B","en":"Configure the Standard Sales Lines page and assign it to a customer record.","es":"Configurar la página Standard Sales Lines y asignarla a un cliente."},{"id":"C","en":"Enter the discount percent in the Line Discount % field.","es":"Introducir el porcentaje en el campo Line Discount %."},{"id":"D","en":"Define the required discount strategy on the Sales & Receivables Setup page.","es":"Definir la estrategia de descuentos en la página Sales & Receivables Setup."},{"id":"E","en":"From the desired item card, navigate to Set Special Discounts.","es":"Desde la ficha del producto, ir a Set Special Discounts."}]},{"id":"s3q48","type":"build","en":"A company uses Dynamics 365 Business Central.<br><br>The company requires the system to prevent sales orders and other sales transactions from posting without a specific dimension, even when no rules are set up for a customer.<br><br>You need to configure the system so customer entries always post with the value for the required dimension.<br><br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"El sistema no debe permitir registrar ventas sin una dimensión concreta, aunque no haya reglas para el cliente.<br><br>¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q48","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Define the dimension value, and in the Value Posting column, set the same dimension value.","es":"Definir el valor y poner Same Code en Value Posting."},{"id":"B","en":"Disable the dimension value from posting.","es":"Impedir el registro del valor de dimensión."},{"id":"C","en":"On the Dimensions page, select the required dimension.","es":"En Dimensions, seleccionar la dimensión."},{"id":"D","en":"Leave the dimension value blank, and in the Value Posting column, select Code Mandatory.","es":"Dejar el valor en blanco y poner Code Mandatory en Value Posting."},{"id":"E","en":"Select the relevant table ID.","es":"Seleccionar el Table ID correspondiente."},{"id":"F","en":"Select Account Type Default Dim.","es":"Seleccionar Account Type Default Dim."}]},{"id":"s3q58","type":"build","en":"A company is implementing Business Central as its business system.<br><br>The company requires the ability to intermittently combine shipments on a single invoice but does not want to automate this feature for any customer.<br><br>You need to demonstrate how to combine shipments manually.<br><br>Which five actions should you perform in sequence?","es":"La empresa quiere combinar envíos en una sola factura de vez en cuando, sin automatizarlo para ningún cliente.<br><br>Debes mostrar cómo hacerlo manualmente. ¿Qué cinco acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Secuencial Topic 3 · Q58","slots":5,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Open the combine shipments batch job request page.","es":"Abrir el proceso Combine Shipments."},{"id":"B","en":"Configure the customer to combine shipments.","es":"Configurar el cliente para combinar envíos."},{"id":"C","en":"Create a new sales invoice.","es":"Crear una factura de venta nueva."},{"id":"D","en":"Select the customer account.","es":"Seleccionar el cliente."},{"id":"E","en":"Get shipment lines.","es":"Ejecutar Get Shipment Lines."},{"id":"F","en":"Select the shipment line(s) that you want to include in the invoice.","es":"Seleccionar los envíos a incluir."},{"id":"G","en":"Post the invoice.","es":"Registrar la factura."}]},{"id":"cs1t3q37","type":"drag","en":"You need to configure Business Central to meet the requirements of the sales department.<br>What should you configure for each setup area? Drag the appropriate configurations to the correct sales and receivables setup.","es":"Debes configurar Business Central según los requisitos del departamento de ventas.<br><br>¿Qué configuración de Sales & Receivables Setup corresponde a cada área?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 3 · Q37","case":"CS1","valuesTitle":"Configurations","targetHeader":["Sales and receivables setup","Configuration"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Credit warnings","es":"Credit warnings"},{"id":"V2","en":"Discount posting","es":"Discount posting"},{"id":"V3","en":"Calc. inv. discount","es":"Calc. inv. discount"},{"id":"V4","en":"Stockout warnings","es":"Stockout warnings"}],"targets":[{"en":"Sales discounts","es":"Descuentos de venta"},{"en":"Credit limits","es":"Límites de crédito"}]},{"id":"cs1t3q38","type":"drag","en":"You need to train the sales department how to correct posted sales invoices.<br>Which action should you use for each scenario?","es":"Debes formar al departamento de ventas en cómo corregir facturas de venta registradas.<br><br>¿Qué acción corresponde a cada escenario?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 3 · Q38","case":"CS1","valuesTitle":"Actions","targetHeader":["Scenario","Action"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Cancel","es":"Cancel"},{"id":"V2","en":"Correct","es":"Correct"},{"id":"V3","en":"Sales return order","es":"Sales return order"},{"id":"V4","en":"Create corrective credit memo","es":"Create corrective credit memo"}],"targets":[{"en":"Use this action when the posted invoice has not been paid and the original invoice was posted from a sales order.","es":"La factura no está pagada y se registró desde un pedido de venta."},{"en":"Use this action when the posted invoice has not been paid and the original invoice was not posted from a sales order.","es":"La factura no está pagada y no se registró desde un pedido de venta."},{"en":"Use this action when the posted invoice has been paid and warehouse documents are not required.","es":"La factura está pagada y no se necesitan documentos de almacén."}]},{"id":"cs1t3q39","type":"mr","en":"You need to set up customer sales pricing based on the requirements.<br>Which three actions should you perform? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Debes configurar los precios de venta a clientes según los requisitos.<br><br>¿Qué tres acciones debes realizar?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 3 · Q39","case":"CS1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create a Sales Price List for the customer by using the customer assign-to type.","es":"Crear una lista de precios de venta para el cliente con assign-to type Customer."},{"id":"B","en":"Create a Sales Price List by using the assign-to type of Customer Price Group.","es":"Crear una lista de precios de venta con assign-to type Customer Price Group."},{"id":"C","en":"Create Customer Price Groups that allow line discounts.","es":"Crear Customer Price Groups que permitan descuentos de línea."},{"id":"D","en":"Assign the Customer Price Group code on the customer card.","es":"Asignar el Customer Price Group en la ficha del cliente."},{"id":"E","en":"Create Customer Price Groups that exclude line discounts.","es":"Crear Customer Price Groups que excluyan los descuentos de línea."}],"select":3},{"id":"cs1t3q43","type":"mr","en":"You need to configure payment discounts to resolve the issue reported by the AR users.<br>Which two options should you configure? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Debes configurar los descuentos por pronto pago para resolver el problema que indican los usuarios de AR.<br><br>¿Qué dos opciones debes configurar?","src":"Case Study 1 · Topic 3 · Q43","case":"CS1","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Sales &amp; Receivables Setup","es":"Sales & Receivables Setup"},{"id":"B","en":"Payment Discount Grace Period","es":"Payment Discount Grace Period"},{"id":"C","en":"Payment Tolerance Warning","es":"Payment Tolerance Warning"},{"id":"D","en":"Pmt. Disc. Tolerance Warning","es":"Pmt. Disc. Tolerance Warning"}],"select":2},{"id":"cs2t3q52","type":"mr","en":"You need to train users on order processing requirements and how to process purchase invoices created from combined receipts.<br>Which two related processes should you include? Each correct answer presents a complete solution.","es":"Debes formar a los usuarios en los requisitos de procesamiento de pedidos y en cómo tratar las facturas de compra creadas a partir de recepciones combinadas.<br><br>¿Qué dos procesos relacionados debes incluir?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 3 · Q52","case":"CS2","options":[{"id":"A","en":"Create recurring purchase lines.","es":"Crear líneas de compra recurrentes."},{"id":"B","en":"Delete POs that are fully invoiced.","es":"Eliminar los pedidos de compra totalmente facturados."},{"id":"C","en":"Create a purchase credit memo.","es":"Crear un abono de compra (purchase credit memo)."},{"id":"D","en":"Correct or cancel unpaid purchase invoices.","es":"Corregir o cancelar facturas de compra no pagadas."}],"select":2},{"id":"cs2t3q53","type":"build","en":"You need to train users on how to process a special order for an established customer.<br>Which four actions should you perform in sequence? (More than one order of answer choices is correct.)","es":"Debes formar a los usuarios en cómo procesar un pedido especial de un cliente ya establecido.<br><br>¿Qué cuatro acciones debes realizar y en qué orden?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 3 · Q53","case":"CS2","slots":4,"actions":[{"id":"A","en":"Enter the code for due on receipt in the prepayment payment terms code.","es":"Indicar el código de pago a la recepción en Prepmt. Payment Terms Code."},{"id":"B","en":"Create a sales order.","es":"Crear un pedido de venta."},{"id":"C","en":"Enter 25 in the Prepayment % field.","es":"Introducir 25 en Prepayment %."},{"id":"D","en":"Enter the code for net 30 in the prepayment payment terms code.","es":"Indicar el código de neto 30 en Prepmt. Payment Terms Code."},{"id":"E","en":"Enter 15 in the Prepayment % field.","es":"Introducir 15 en Prepayment %."},{"id":"F","en":"Post and print the invoice.","es":"Registrar e imprimir la factura."},{"id":"G","en":"Post and print the prepayment invoice.","es":"Registrar e imprimir la factura de anticipo."}]},{"id":"cs2t3q54","type":"drag","en":"You need to resolve the order entry issue.<br>How should you complete each action? Move the appropriate recurring sales line configurations to the correct actions.","es":"Debes resolver el problema de entrada de pedidos.<br><br>¿Qué configuración de líneas de venta recurrentes corresponde a cada acción?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 3 · Q54","case":"CS2","valuesTitle":"Recurring sales line configurations","targetHeader":["Action","Recurring sales line configuration"],"values":[{"id":"V1","en":"Add items and quantities.","es":"Añadir artículos y cantidades."},{"id":"V2","en":"Add valid from and to dates.","es":"Añadir fechas de validez desde/hasta."},{"id":"V3","en":"Set insert on orders to Always Ask.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Orders en Always Ask."},{"id":"V4","en":"Set insert on quotes to Automatic.","es":"Poner Insert Rec. Lines on Quotes en Automatic."}],"targets":[{"en":"Configure standard sales lines.","es":"Configurar las Standard Sales Lines."},{"en":"Add recurring sales lines to customers.","es":"Añadir líneas de venta recurrentes a los clientes."}]},{"id":"cs2t3q55","type":"hotspot","en":"You need to complete inventory setup in Business Central to meet requirements and resolve issues.<br>Which two inventory setup configurations should you use?","es":"Debes completar la configuración de inventario para cumplir los requisitos y resolver los problemas.<br><br>¿Qué configuración de Inventory Setup corresponde a cada acción?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 3 · Q55","case":"CS2","rowsHeader":["Inventory setup action","Configuration"],"rows":[{"en":"Set the default costing method.","es":"Fijar el costing method por defecto.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Average","es":"Average"},{"id":"b","en":"FIFO","es":"FIFO"},{"id":"c","en":"Specific","es":"Specific"},{"id":"d","en":"Standard","es":"Standard"}]},{"en":"Resolve inventory reconciliation issue.","es":"Resolver el problema de conciliación de inventario.","options":[{"id":"a","en":"Automatic cost posting","es":"Automatic cost posting"},{"id":"b","en":"Automatic cost adjustment","es":"Automatic cost adjustment"},{"id":"c","en":"Allow inventory adjustment","es":"Allow inventory adjustment"},{"id":"d","en":"Prevent negative inventory","es":"Prevent negative inventory"}]}]},{"id":"cs2t3q56","type":"mr","en":"You need to configure posting groups to post revenue per invoicing requirements.<br>Which two groups should you use? Each correct answer presents part of the solution.","es":"Debes configurar los posting groups para registrar los ingresos según los requisitos de facturación.<br><br>¿Qué dos grupos debes usar?","src":"Case Study 2 · Topic 3 · Q56","case":"CS2","options":[{"id":"A","en":"bank account posting groups","es":"bank account posting groups"},{"id":"B","en":"general business posting groups","es":"general business posting groups"},{"id":"C","en":"customer posting groups","es":"customer posting groups"},{"id":"D","en":"general product posting groups","es":"general product posting groups"},{"id":"E","en":"inventory posting groups","es":"inventory posting groups"}],"select":2}]};
